Z||000002||RobertVol||05-04-2000||12:42 AM||||I agree! My first car when I turned 16 was a brand new 87 Blue with the grey bottom GT fastback. With the 5 speed! Why now after all these years do you think I am here?!?! I fell in love and years later had to have more of them. That Blue left avery LASTING impression||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wannabe||05-04-2000||12:57 AM||||I've been looking for a decent '86 or up 5 spd GT and have found what might be good deal. It's an '87 GT 5 spd with about 80k miles for under $2000. Salt free and "lady driven" by the original owner. It also happens to have the original blue paint, which was not my color of choice. Hopefully it will grow on me because it wouldn't feel right covering up a "special" color with red,  my "special" color  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> In a couple of days, I might not be "Wannabe" any more!||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||05-04-2000||03:49 AM||||One word GO-FOR-IT!! 87 Blue gts are very very nice. Not very many made either. Don't you dare paint it another color.  Does it have a wing??? Also if it is nice shape, that is a great price.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||05-04-2000||09:59 AM||||Hey Wannabe,<P>Is that $2000 Canadian or U.S.? Either way, if the car is clean then it's a steal. If yo decide not to buy, there may be someone on this list who will. Just let us know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Also, I checked out your web page. Looks like someone else is into custom gauge colors. Welcome to the group.<P>Roy L.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Wannabe||05-04-2000||10:47 PM||||Ok, I bought it! It's not what you would call cherry, but it is generally in good shape. There is no broken trim in the interior, no cracks on the dash and everything works except the parking brake. New clutch, 86k miles, new brakes, and the suspension feels generally tight (not that that matters as I will be stripping down anyway) It is going to take some work and lots of liquid wrench to get things moving. I talked the price down some to make it a deal I couldn't pass up.Elbow grease, paint and a good scrubbing should make it nice and pretty. The blue, well, it might grow on me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||RossT||05-04-2000||11:35 PM||||Ok, now go take some pictures, post them and change your username.  Congradulations!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ozzy||05-06-2000||04:04 AM||||Good deal dude! I recently bought a blue '87 GT. I paid $2600 for mine. 120k, AC, PM, PW, 5spd, tilt. Had a aftermarket stereo and rims though. Needs some work but find me a Fiero that dont. Paint is real clean and has grey ground FX too. <P><BR>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000009||CUTTER||05-07-2000||07:01 PM||||I bought a blue 87GT last year for $1500 US had 75000 miles, power everything, everything worked, ac, at, sunroof, performance sound, no body damage, ran strong. The only thing was paint faded on the roof, but im in the process of repainting it now. I didnt know how good of a price I got untill I came on this forum and other people were saying $2500-$3000 was a steal for a car like I had!||||reg||14
